sequenceDiagram
    title BLE GATT Disconnect During Pending Operation

    participant App as App<br>[implements GattClientResponse, GapCentralResponse]
    participant Node as Node<br>[implements GattClient, GapCentral]
    participant Peripheral as BLE Peripheral

    Note over Node, Peripheral: Messages between Node and BLE Peripheral<br>are link-layer / ATT events, not driven by the App.<br>The App only observes them through Echo callbacks.
    Note over App, Node: Any pending GATT operation is implicitly cancelled on<br>connection loss and its "Expected response" is delivered<br>with an error status.

    App->>Node: GattClient.ReadCharacteristic(0x0025)
    Node-)Peripheral: ATT_READ_REQ (handle=0x0025)

    rect rgb(245, 230, 230)
        Peripheral-)Node: LL_TERMINATE_IND
    end

    Node-->>App: GattClientResponse.OperationComplete(error)
    Node-->>App: GapCentralResponse.CurrentState(standby)
    Note over App, Node: OperationComplete(error) is delivered before CurrentState(standby).<br>No further GATT callbacks fire until the App re-establishes the link<br>and re-drives discovery from ServiceDiscovery.
